Galactic Empire Planet Configuration Table
Version ge-next 0.4

LEVEL4 {}

Creation templates for the neutral zone and faction outposts.
Changing a template does not change objects already saved in the database.

Format PLANETS1: each section has a stable section tag, one to nine object
definitions, and an END marker. DONE terminates the file. Section tags identify
layouts, not their displayed planet names. Each of the six sections is required.

Each object has exactly eight options, in this order:
TYP, NM, OWN, X, Y, ENV, RES, OUT. Do not insert other options within an object.
Add or remove complete object blocks before the section END marker; there are
no DEF switches, explicit counts or reserved object slots. Keep option names
unique. The game reads section/type values and option order, not option names.
Keep PLTSTART first and do not change its name. Recreate MPOGEPLT.MCV after
editing; adding objects does not require recompiling the DLL.

TYP: PLANET or WORMHOLE. END has no following object fields.
NM: displayed name, up to 19 characters. OWN: legacy owner display text.
Faction ownership comes from the section, not OWN or the displayed name.
X/Y: local coordinates, 100 through 9900 (5000 is the sector center).
ENV/RES: 0 = Poor, 1 = Marginal, 2 = Good, 3 = Very good.
OUT: 0 = None, 1 = Zygor, 2 = Tahanian, 3 = Enforcer, 4 = Lydoria,
5 = Sarten, 6 = Murdonia, 7 = Vakory, 8 = Zygor Express. Wormholes use 0.

Sector 0 0 object 1 must be the Zygor planet (role 1). Each other section
must start with its primary outpost planet and matching role. Objects receive
consecutive numbers in file order. Express uses the same layout at all four
locations and is not created when UNIVMAX is below 50.

PLTSTART {PLANETS1} E PLANETS1

S00SECT {NEUTRAL} E NEUTRAL

S00P1TYP {Object kind: PLANET} E PLANET WORMHOLE END
S00P1NM {Zygor} S 19 Planet #1 Name
S00P1OWN {*Galactic Command*} S 29 Owner of Planet #1
S00P1X {X Coordinate of Planet: 5000} N 100 9900
S00P1Y {Y Coordinate of Planet: 5000} N 100 9900
S00P1ENV {Environment for planet: 3} N 0 3
S00P1RES {Resources for planet: 3} N 0 3
S00P1OUT {Outpost role: 1} N 0 8

